+## Dated book references (context only, never a threshold or verdict)
+
+| Reference | Figure | Grade · date · scope |
+|---|---|---|
+| Trial starts (Lean Analytics, Totango) | 0.5–2% of visitors with card vs 5–10% without; first-bill churn up to 40% vs 20% | C · c. 2012 · venture SaaS |
+| SaaS monthly churn (Lean Analytics) | Best 1.5–3%; under 5% before scaling | C · 2009–2012 · venture SaaS |
+| Ecommerce repurchase mode (Hillstrom, in Lean Analytics) | Annual repurchase <40% acquisition, 40–60% hybrid, >60% loyalty; loyalty programs rarely pay in acquisition mode | C · c. 2012 · one consultant, no sample |
+| Buyer concentration (How Brands Grow 1–2) | Top 20% of buyers ≈ 40–60% of annual volume, not 80%; about half of one period's heaviest aren't heavy the next | B · 2010–2016 · consumer repeat; not B2B account revenue |
+| Perceived differentiation (How Brands Grow) | ~10% of a brand's users call it different or unique | B · ≤2014 · consumer and bank surveys |
+| Temporary price cuts (How Brands Grow) | Elasticity usually −1 to −4, average about −2.5 | B · ≤2014 · consumer goods |
